{{Quote|A jungle world. Domed cities I see. Rodia it is.|[[Yoda]]|<ref name="CotF" />}}
'''Rodia''' was a remote and [[swamp]]y [[jungle]] [[planet]]. It was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Rodian]] [[species]].<ref name="data" /> [[City|Cities]] on Rodia were encased with domed environmental shields that allowed entry and exit for vehicles and vessels.<ref name="TCW-BJ" />

==Description==
Located on the border between the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] and the [[Outer Rim Territories]], and the second [[orbit]] in the five-[[planet]] [[Tyrius system]], the planet Rodia was in a region of [[the galaxy]] that had been very busy throughout history. The primary world in the [[Savareen sector]]<ref name="BMF 58" /> at grid square R-16<ref name="Galaxy Map" /> on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]],<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref> Rodia was situated close to the [[Corellian Run]] [[super-hyperroute]], which gave travelers a clear route all the way throughout the [[galaxy]]. A hotbed of life with a [[Temperature|hot]] and humid climate and breathable [[atmosphere]], Rodia was mostly covered in [[water]], including the vast [[Wesessa Sea]]. The majority of the planet's solid landmasses that were not submerged were covered in unworkable [[swamp]]s, thick [[forest]]s and [[jungle]]s, with colder regions to the north and south of the planet.<ref name="BMF 58" /> Rodia had a strong smell that was pungent to most visitors.<ref name="Heir to the Jedi" />

==History==
===Union with the Galactic Republic===
Around [[15,000 BBY|fifteen millennia]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], Rodia had joined the [[Galactic Republic]] after seeing benefits come from their union. New technology had made its way onto the planet and, with permission from the [[Grand Protector]], Rodian [[hunter]]s were allowed to leave Rodia&mdash;an act which was impermissible previously&mdash;and embark upon galaxy-wide careers as [[bounty hunter]]s, [[enslaver]]s and [[soldier]]s of fortune.<ref name="BMF 58" />

===Republic's final days===
[[File:Rodia_palace.png|thumb|left|230px|Bubble-domed habitats on Rodia]]
Later, during the [[Republic Era|waning days]] of the Republic, the planet was represented in the [[Galactic Senate]] by [[Senator]] [[Onaconda Farr]]. Republic supply [[Starship|ships]] en route to Rodia were destroyed by [[pirate]]s, leading to many Rodians starving. At some point during the [[Clone Wars]], Farr betrayed his old friend and ally Senator [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] by [[Mission to Rodia|luring]] her to Rodia and into the clutches of her old enemy, the [[Trade Federation]] [[Viceroy of the Trade Federation|viceroy]], [[Nute Gunray]], in exchange for the shipment of supplies, which the Republic had failed to deliver to his planet. However, when Gunray stated his intentions to execute Amidala, and delay the delivery of Rodia's supplies, he realized his mistake and helped her escape. The two held Gunray at gunpoint and had him arrested. [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] dispatched several supply convoys to Rodia upon learning of the dilemma.<ref name="TCW-BJ" />

At some point, [[Jedi Knight]]s [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker]] crashed their [[BTL Y-wing starfighter|Y-wing]] into a shield protecting a [[city]] near the [[Senatorial Palace]] as they were [[Investigation on Rodia|looking]] into the actions of some [[Unidentified rogue Nightsisters|rogue Nightsisters]] on the planet. When the shield was abruptly activated, the starfighter was entirely destroyed, while the dome remained unaffected.<ref name ="Mustafar and Other">{{EncyclopediaCite|Mustafar and Other Planets in the Outer Rim}}</ref> Bounty hunter [[Cad Bane]] was later [[Second mission to Rodia|assigned]] to Rodia by Darth Sidious to capture a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Wee Dunn|Rodian child]]. [[Jedi General]] Obi-Wan Kenobi arrived too late to prevent the child's kidnapping.<ref name="CotF" /> [[Ahsoka Tano]] later recalled the incident during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="FOTF">{{Rebels|The Future of the Force}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
The [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] created a swelling clan rivalry in Rodian society, culminating in [[Navik's insurrection]].<ref name="BMF58">{{BuildFalconCite|58|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref>

By the [[time]] of the [[Galactic Civil War]], Rodia had fallen under [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] control. Many Rodians who opposed the occupation of their homeworld were recruited by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> Shortly after the destruction of the first [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]], [[Luke Skywalker]] took a luxury [[yacht]], the ''[[Desert Jewel]]'', to Rodia's [[Betu]] continent on a secret [[Mission to Rodia (Luke Skywalker)|mission]] to recruit the [[Chekkoo clan]] to the Alliance to Restore the Republic. The Chekkoo clan opposed the ruling [[Chattza clan]], which sided with the Empire. In his stay on Rodia, he learned of a Rodian [[Jedi]] named [[Huulik]] who fought in the Clone Wars and visited a [[Huulik's mausoleum|secret mausoleum]] deep in the jungle to honor Huulik.<ref name="Heir to the Jedi" />

Around the time of the [[Battle of Jakku]], Rodia was represented in the [[New Republic Senate|Galactic Senate]] of the [[New Republic]] by [[Dor Wieedo]].<ref name="Empire's End" />

==Behind the scenes==
Rodia first appeared in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] novel [[Star Wars: Shadows of the Empire (novel)|''Shadows of the Empire'']], which was written by [[Steve Perry]] and published in [[1996]].<ref name="Shadows">[[Star Wars: Shadows of the Empire (novel)|''Star Wars: Shadows of the Empire'' novel]]</ref>. It first appeared in [[canon]] in an opening flashback in "[[Ambush]]," an episode of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' that first aired on [[October 3]], [[2008]].<ref name="Ambush Ep Guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode001.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Ambush}}</ref>

